{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol | sed -n '360,475p'\nnl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/Context.sol | sed -n '1,120p'\nnl -ba packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol | sed -n '1,210p'\nrg -n \\\"contract Raffle|approve\\\\(|_approve\\\\(|isApprovedForAll|_ownerOf|_requireOwned|_msgSender|ERC721\\\\(\\\" packages/contracts/src packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721 packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/Context.sol\"","aggregated_output":"   360\t    function _safeTransfer(address from, address to, uint256 tokenId, bytes memory data) internal virtual {\n   361\t        _transfer(from, to, tokenId);\n   362\t        ERC721Utils.checkOnERC721Received(_msgSender(), from, to, tokenId, data);\n   363\t    }\n   364\t\n   365\t    /**\n   366\t     * @dev Approve `to` to operate on `tokenId`\n   367\t     *\n   368\t     * The `auth` argument is optional. If the value passed is non 0, then this function will check that `auth` is\n   369\t     * either the owner of the token, or approved to operate on all tokens held by this owner.\n   370\t     *\n   371\t     * Emits an {Approval} event.\n   372\t     *\n   373\t     * Overrides to this logic should be done to the variant with an additional `bool emitEvent` argument.\n   374\t     */\n   375\t    function _approve(address to, uint256 tokenId, address auth) internal {\n   376\t        _approve(to, tokenId, auth, true);\n   377\t    }\n   378\t\n   379\t    /**\n   380\t     * @dev Variant of `_approve` with an optional flag to enable or disable the {Approval} event. The event is not\n   381\t     * emitted in the context of transfers.\n   382\t     */\n   383\t    function _approve(address to, uint256 tokenId, address auth, bool emitEvent) internal virtual {\n   384\t        // Avoid reading the owner unless necessary\n   385\t        if (emitEvent || auth != address(0)) {\n   386\t            address owner = _requireOwned(tokenId);\n   387\t\n   388\t            // We do not use _isAuthorized because single-token approvals should not be able to call approve\n   389\t            if (auth != address(0) && owner != auth && !isApprovedForAll(owner, auth)) {\n   390\t                revert ERC721InvalidApprover(auth);\n   391\t            }\n   392\t\n   393\t            if (emitEvent) {\n   394\t                emit Approval(owner, to, tokenId);\n   395\t            }\n   396\t        }\n   397\t\n   398\t        _tokenApprovals[tokenId] = to;\n   399\t    }\n   400\t\n   401\t    /**\n   402\t     * @dev Approve `operator` to operate on all of `owner` tokens\n   403\t     *\n   404\t     * Requirements:\n   405\t     * - operator can't be the address zero.\n   406\t     *\n   407\t     * Emits an {ApprovalForAll} event.\n   408\t     */\n   409\t    function _setApprovalForAll(address owner, address operator, bool approved) internal virtual {\n   410\t        if (owner == address(0)) {\n   411\t            revert ERC721InvalidApprover(address(0));\n   412\t        }\n   413\t        if (operator == address(0)) {\n   414\t            revert ERC721InvalidOperator(operator);\n   415\t        }\n   416\t        _operatorApprovals[owner][operator] = approved;\n   417\t        emit ApprovalForAll(owner, operator, approved);\n   418\t    }\n   419\t\n   420\t    /**\n   421\t     * @dev Reverts if the `tokenId` doesn't have a current owner (it hasn't been minted, or it has been burned).\n   422\t     * Returns the owner.\n   423\t     *\n   424\t     * Overrides to ownership logic should be done to {_ownerOf}.\n   425\t     */\n   426\t    function _requireOwned(uint256 tokenId) internal view returns (address) {\n   427\t        address owner = _ownerOf(tokenId);\n   428\t        if (owner == address(0)) {\n   429\t            revert ERC721NonexistentToken(tokenId);\n   430\t        }\n   431\t        return owner;\n   432\t    }\n   433\t}\n     1\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     2\t// OpenZeppelin Contracts (last updated v5.0.1) (utils/Context.sol)\n     3\t\n     4\tpragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n     5\t\n     6\t/**\n     7\t * @dev Provides information about the current execution context, including the\n     8\t * sender of the transaction and its data. While these are generally available\n     9\t * via msg.sender and msg.data, they should not be accessed in such a direct\n    10\t * manner, since when dealing with meta-transactions the account sending and\n    11\t * paying for execution may not be the actual sender (as far as an application\n    12\t * is concerned).\n    13\t *\n    14\t * This contract is only required for intermediate, library-like contracts.\n    15\t */\n    16\tabstract contract Context {\n    17\t    function _msgSender() internal view virtual returns (address) {\n    18\t        return msg.sender;\n    19\t    }\n    20\t\n    21\t    function _msgData() internal view virtual returns (bytes calldata) {\n    22\t        return msg.data;\n    23\t    }\n    24\t\n    25\t    function _contextSuffixLength() internal view virtual returns (uint256) {\n    26\t        return 0;\n    27\t    }\n    28\t}\n     1\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     2\tpragma solidity 0.8.36;\n     3\t\n     4\timport { VRFV2PlusWrapperConsumerBase } from \"@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/VRFV2PlusWrapperConsumerBase.sol\";\n     5\timport { IVRFV2PlusWrapper } from \"@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/interfaces/IVRFV2PlusWrapper.sol\";\n     6\timport { VRFV2PlusClient } from \"@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/libraries/VRFV2PlusClient.sol\";\n     7\timport { IERC20 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\n     8\timport { SafeERC20 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol\";\n     9\timport { ERC721 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol\";\n    10\timport { IERC721 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol\";\n    11\timport { IERC721Receiver } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721Receiver.sol\";\n    12\timport { ReentrancyGuard } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol\";\n    13\timport { Math } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/math/Math.sol\";\n    14\t\n    15\timport { IRaffle } from \"./interfaces/IRaffle.sol\";\n    16\timport { IRaffleFactory } from \"./interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol\";\n    17\timport { RaffleConstants } from \"./libraries/RaffleConstants.sol\";\n    18\t\n    19\t/// @title raffle.fun Raffle Escrow and Entry Ticket\n    20\t/// @author heesho\n    21\t/// @notice Escrows one NFT and sells fixed-price USDC entries through one transferable ERC-721 ticket per purchase.\n    22\t/// @dev Ticket IDs are sequential and map to one inclusive `[firstEntry,lastEntry]` uint128 range. Purchases, Chainlink\n    23\t///      callbacks, and winner proofs are O(1) in entry count. Tickets remain transferable bearer claims until their\n    24\t///      owners burn them for redemption or refund. Each raffle is a fixed, non-upgradeable ERC-1167 clone with no\n    25\t///      administrator or rescue path. Permissionless settlement only allocates liabilities; the winning-ticket owner\n    26\t///      atomically burns the ticket while receiving the NFT or cash prize.\n    27\t/// @custom:version 1.0.0\n    28\tcontract Raffle is IRaffle, ERC721, ReentrancyGuard, IERC721Receiver, VRFV2PlusWrapperConsumerBase {\n    29\t    using SafeERC20 for IERC20;\n    30\t\n    31\t    // Types\n    32\t\n    33\t    /// @notice Inclusive global entry-number range represented by one sequential ERC-721 ticket.\n    34\t    /// @param firstEntry First represented one-based global entry.\n    35\t    /// @param lastEntry Last represented one-based global entry.\n    36\t    struct TicketRange {\n    37\t        uint128 firstEntry;\n    38\t        uint128 lastEntry;\n    39\t    }\n    40\t\n    41\t    // Constants\n    42\t\n    43\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    44\t    uint256 public constant override ENTRY_PRICE = RaffleConstants.ENTRY_PRICE;\n    45\t\n    46\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    47\t    uint32 public constant override callbackGasLimit = RaffleConstants.VRF_CALLBACK_GAS_LIMIT;\n    48\t\n    49\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    50\t    uint16 public constant override requestConfirmations = RaffleConstants.VRF_REQUEST_CONFIRMATIONS;\n    51\t\n    52\t    // Immutables and state\n    53\t\n    54\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    55\t    address public immutable override factory;\n    56\t\n    57\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    58\t    IERC20 public immutable override quoteToken;\n    59\t\n    60\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    61\t    address public override sponsor;\n    62\t\n    63\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    64\t    address public override sponsorRecipient;\n    65\t\n    66\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    67\t    address public override protocolTreasury;\n    68\t\n    69\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    70\t    IERC721 public override prizeToken;\n    71\t\n    72\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    73\t    uint256 public override prizeTokenId;\n    74\t\n    75\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    76\t    uint256 public override raffleId;\n    77\t\n    78\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    79\t    uint128 public override reserveEntries;\n    80\t\n    81\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    82\t    uint64 public override endTime;\n    83\t\n    84\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    85\t    uint128 public override totalEntries;\n    86\t\n    87\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    88\t    uint128 public override ticketCount;\n    89\t\n    90\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    91\t    uint256 public override unsettledPot;\n    92\t\n    93\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    94\t    uint256 public override remainingRefundLiability;\n    95\t\n    96\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    97\t    address public override winnerRecipient;\n    98\t\n    99\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   100\t    uint256 public override winnerProceeds;\n   101\t\n   102\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   103\t    uint256 public override sponsorProceeds;\n   104\t\n   105\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   106\t    uint256 public override protocolFees;\n   107\t\n   108\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   109\t    uint256 public override vrfRequestId;\n   110\t\n   111\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   112\t    uint64 public override drawRequestedAt;\n   113\t\n   114\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   115\t    uint64 public override resolvedAt;\n   116\t\n   117\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   118\t    uint128 public override winningEntry;\n   119\t\n   120\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   121\t    uint256 public override winningTicketId;\n   122\t\n   123\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   124\t    Status public override status;\n   125\t\n   126\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   127\t    bool public override settlementComplete;\n   128\t\n   129\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   130\t    bool public override winnerRedeemed;\n   131\t\n   132\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   133\t    bool public override prizeClaimed;\n   134\t\n   135\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   136\t    bool public override initialized;\n   137\t\n   138\t    /// @dev Historical ticket ranges remain stored after burns so indexers and callers can reconstruct entry coverage.\n   139\t    mapping(uint256 ticketId => TicketRange range) private _ticketRanges;\n   140\t\n   141\t    /// @dev True only while the wrapper request call is executing, so a synchronous callback cannot resolve early.\n   142\t    bool private _requestInFlight;\n   143\t\n   144\t    // Errors\n   145\t\n   146\t    /// @notice Raised when native currency is sent outside the payable draw-request path.\n   147\t    error DirectNativeTransfer();\n   148\t\n   149\t    // Constructor\n   150\t\n   151\t    /// @notice Deploys and locks the implementation shared by one factory's minimal-proxy raffles.\n   152\t    /// @dev Constructor state belongs to the implementation. Clones share these immutables but hold isolated storage.\n   153\t    /// @param quoteToken_ Canonical six-decimal USDC contract fixed for the implementation and every clone.\n   154\t    /// @param vrfWrapper_ Chainlink VRF v2.5 native direct-funding wrapper fixed for the implementation and all clones.\n   155\t    constructor(address quoteToken_, address vrfWrapper_)\n   156\t        ERC721(\"\", \"\")\n   157\t        VRFV2PlusWrapperConsumerBase(_validatedVrfWrapper(vrfWrapper_))\n   158\t    {\n   159\t        if (msg.sender == address(0) || quoteToken_ == address(0)) revert ZeroAddress();\n   160\t\n   161\t        factory = msg.sender;\n   162\t        quoteToken = IERC20(quoteToken_);\n   163\t\n   164\t        initialized = true;\n   165\t        status = Status.Refunding;\n   166\t    }\n   167\t\n   168\t    // External state-changing functions\n   169\t\n   170\t    /// @notice Rejects direct native-token transfers that are not attached to `requestDraw`.\n   171\t    receive() external payable {\n   172\t        revert DirectNativeTransfer();\n   173\t    }\n   174\t\n   175\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   176\t    function initialize(RaffleInitParams calldata params) external override {\n   177\t        if (initialized) revert AlreadyInitialized();\n   178\t        if (msg.sender != factory) revert OnlyFactory();\n   179\t        initialized = true;\n   180\t\n   181\t        if (\n   182\t            params.sponsor == address(0) || params.sponsorRecipient == address(0)\n   183\t                || params.protocolTreasury == address(0) || params.prizeToken == address(0)\n   184\t        ) {\n   185\t            revert ZeroAddress();\n   186\t        }\n   187\t        if (_isProtocolDestination(params.sponsor, params.prizeToken)) {\n   188\t            revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(params.sponsor);\n   189\t        }\n   190\t        if (_isProtocolDestination(params.protocolTreasury, params.prizeToken)) {\n   191\t            revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(params.protocolTreasury);\n   192\t        }\n   193\t        if (_isProtocolDestination(params.sponsorRecipient, params.prizeToken)) {\n   194\t            revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(params.sponsorRecipient);\n   195\t        }\n   196\t\n   197\t        sponsor = params.sponsor;\n   198\t        sponsorRecipient = params.sponsorRecipient;\n   199\t        protocolTreasury = params.protocolTreasury;\n   200\t        prizeToken = IERC721(params.prizeToken);\n   201\t        prizeTokenId = params.prizeTokenId;\n   202\t        raffleId = params.raffleId;\n   203\t        reserveEntries = params.reserveEntries;\n   204\t        endTime = params.endTime;\n   205\t        status = Status.AwaitingPrize;\n   206\t    }\n   207\t\n   208\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n   209\t    function buyEntries(address recipient, uint128 entryCount)\n   210\t        external\npackages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:21:contract RaffleFactory is IRaffleFactory, ReentrancyGuard {\npackages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:127:        IERC721 prize = IERC721(params.prizeToken);\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:28:contract Raffle is IRaffle, ERC721, ReentrancyGuard, IERC721Receiver, VRFV2PlusWrapperConsumerBase {\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:156:        ERC721(\"\", \"\")\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:200:        prizeToken = IERC721(params.prizeToken);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:62:        return _requireOwned(tokenId);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:77:        _requireOwned(tokenId);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:93:    function approve(address to, uint256 tokenId) public virtual {\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:94:        _approve(to, tokenId, _msgSender());\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:99:        _requireOwned(tokenId);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:106:        _setApprovalForAll(_msgSender(), operator, approved);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:110:    function isApprovedForAll(address owner, address operator) public view virtual returns (bool) {\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:121:        address previousOwner = _update(to, tokenId, _msgSender());\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:135:        ERC721Utils.checkOnERC721Received(_msgSender(), from, to, tokenId, data);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:144:     * `balanceOf(a)` must be equal to the number of tokens such that `_ownerOf(tokenId)` is `a`.\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:146:    function _ownerOf(uint256 tokenId) internal view virtual returns (address) {\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:167:            (owner == spender || isApprovedForAll(owner, spender) || _getApproved(tokenId) == spender);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:196:     * {_ownerOf} function to resolve the ownership of the corresponding tokens so that balances and ownership\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:217:        address from = _ownerOf(tokenId);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:227:            _approve(address(0), tokenId, address(0), false);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:289:        ERC721Utils.checkOnERC721Received(_msgSender(), address(0), to, tokenId, data);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:362:        ERC721Utils.checkOnERC721Received(_msgSender(), from, to, tokenId, data);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:375:    function _approve(address to, uint256 tokenId, address auth) internal {\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:376:        _approve(to, tokenId, auth, true);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:383:    function _approve(address to, uint256 tokenId, address auth, bool emitEvent) internal virtual {\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:386:            address owner = _requireOwned(tokenId);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:389:            if (auth != address(0) && owner != auth && !isApprovedForAll(owner, auth)) {\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:424:     * Overrides to ownership logic should be done to {_ownerOf}.\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:426:    function _requireOwned(uint256 tokenId) internal view returns (address) {\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:427:        address owner = _ownerOf(tokenId);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol:106:    function approve(address to, uint256 tokenId) external;\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol:134:    function isApprovedForAll(address owner, address operator) external view returns (bool);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/Context.sol:17:    function _msgSender() internal view virtual returns (address) {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
