{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol | sed -n '1,220p'\nnl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol | sed -n '80,145p'\nrg -n \\\"interface IRaffle|IERC721\\\" packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     2\tpragma solidity 0.8.36;\n     3\t\n     4\timport { IVRFV2PlusWrapper } from \"@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/interfaces/IVRFV2PlusWrapper.sol\";\n     5\timport { IERC20 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\n     6\timport { IERC721 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol\";\n     7\t\n     8\t/// @title raffle.fun Raffle Interface\n     9\t/// @author heesho\n    10\t/// @notice Defines one autonomous NFT raffle using fixed-price USDC entries and one transferable ERC-721 ticket per\n    11\t///         purchase.\n    12\t/// @dev Ticket IDs are sequential. Each ticket stores one inclusive uint128 entry range and remains a transferable\n    13\t///      bearer claim until its owner atomically burns it for redemption or refund. The immutable quote token is trusted\n    14\t///      canonical six-decimal USDC with standard, non-rebasing, fee-free transfers. Supported prizes are honest,\n    15\t///      standards-compliant ERC-721s.\n    16\t/// @custom:version 1.0.0\n    17\tinterface IRaffle {\n    18\t    // Types\n    19\t\n    20\t    /// @notice The single authoritative raffle lifecycle and economic result.\n    21\t    enum Status {\n    22\t        /// @notice The clone is initialized and waiting for the factory to escrow the configured prize.\n    23\t        AwaitingPrize,\n    24\t        /// @notice The prize is escrowed and entry sales or post-sale draw initiation are available.\n    25\t        Active,\n    26\t        /// @notice A Chainlink VRF request was accepted and its callback window is open.\n    27\t        Drawing,\n    28\t        /// @notice The reserve was met and the winning ticket may redeem the prize NFT.\n    29\t        NftWon,\n    30\t        /// @notice The reserve was missed and the winning ticket may redeem its cash allocation.\n    31\t        CashWon,\n    32\t        /// @notice Full ticket refunds are enabled and the sponsor may recover the prize NFT.\n    33\t        Refunding\n    34\t    }\n    35\t\n    36\t    /// @notice Complete clone-specific configuration supplied once by the canonical factory.\n    37\t    /// @param sponsor Prize depositor and empty-raffle cancellation authority.\n    38\t    /// @param sponsorRecipient Immutable recipient of sponsor quote proceeds and any returned prize.\n    39\t    /// @param protocolTreasury Immutable recipient of protocol fees.\n    40\t    /// @param prizeToken Standards-compliant ERC-721 prize contract.\n    41\t    /// @param prizeTokenId Token ID of the prize escrowed by this raffle.\n    42\t    /// @param raffleId One-based canonical factory identifier for this raffle.\n    43\t    /// @param reserveEntries Global raw entry-count threshold selecting the NFT outcome when met or exceeded.\n    44\t    /// @param endTime Unix timestamp, in seconds, at which entry sales end exclusively.\n    45\t    struct RaffleInitParams {\n    46\t        address sponsor;\n    47\t        address sponsorRecipient;\n    48\t        address protocolTreasury;\n    49\t        address prizeToken;\n    50\t        uint256 prizeTokenId;\n    51\t        uint256 raffleId;\n    52\t        uint128 reserveEntries;\n    53\t        uint64 endTime;\n    54\t    }\n    55\t\n    56\t    // Events\n    57\t\n    58\t    /// @notice Emitted when the factory deposits the configured prize and activates the raffle.\n    59\t    /// @param prizeToken ERC-721 contract of the deposited prize.\n    60\t    /// @param prizeTokenId Token ID of the deposited prize.\n    61\t    /// @param sponsor Address that deposited the prize through the factory.\n    62\t    event PrizeDeposited(address indexed prizeToken, uint256 indexed prizeTokenId, address indexed sponsor);\n    63\t\n    64\t    /// @notice Emitted when a buyer pays for entries and one range ticket is minted.\n    65\t    /// @param buyer Address that paid the six-decimal quote-token amount.\n    66\t    /// @param recipient Address that received the newly minted ticket.\n    67\t    /// @param ticketId Sequential ticket ID assigned to the purchase.\n    68\t    /// @param firstEntry First global raffle entry represented by the ticket, inclusive.\n    69\t    /// @param lastEntry Last global raffle entry represented by the ticket, inclusive.\n    70\t    /// @param entryCount Number of entries represented by the ticket.\n    71\t    /// @param grossAmount Raw six-decimal quote-token units paid, equal to `entryCount * ENTRY_PRICE`.\n    72\t    event TicketPurchased(\n    73\t        address indexed buyer,\n    74\t        address indexed recipient,\n    75\t        uint256 indexed ticketId,\n    76\t        uint128 firstEntry,\n    77\t        uint128 lastEntry,\n    78\t        uint128 entryCount,\n    79\t        uint256 grossAmount\n    80\t    );\n    81\t\n    82\t    /// @notice Emitted when the raffle pays for and records its one Chainlink VRF request.\n    83\t    /// @param requestId Wrapper-assigned request identifier.\n    84\t    /// @param requester Address that initiated and funded the request.\n    85\t    /// @param fee Native-token wei actually paid to the wrapper for the request.\n    86\t    /// @param excessReturned Native-token wei returned to the requester after paying the actual fee.\n    87\t    /// @param drawRequestedAt Unix timestamp, in seconds, when the request was accepted.\n    88\t    /// @param callbackDeadline Exclusive Unix-timestamp deadline for accepting the authenticated callback.\n    89\t    event DrawRequested(\n    90\t        uint256 indexed requestId,\n    91\t        address indexed requester,\n    92\t        uint256 fee,\n    93\t        uint256 excessReturned,\n    94\t        uint256 drawRequestedAt,\n    95\t        uint256 callbackDeadline\n    96\t    );\n    97\t\n    98\t    /// @notice Emitted when an authenticated, ABI-decodable callback cannot resolve the raffle.\n    99\t    /// @param receivedRequestId Request ID supplied by the wrapper callback.\n   100\t    /// @param expectedRequestId Request ID currently recorded by the raffle, or zero before request persistence.\n   101\t    /// @param status Current raffle status when the callback is ignored.\n   102\t    event VrfCallbackIgnored(uint256 indexed receivedRequestId, uint256 indexed expectedRequestId, Status status);\n   103\t\n   104\t    /// @notice Emitted when an authenticated callback selects the winning entry and final result.\n   105\t    /// @param requestId Request ID that produced the accepted randomness.\n   106\t    /// @param winningEntry Selected one-based global entry number in `[1,totalEntries]`.\n   107\t    /// @param result Final `NftWon` or `CashWon` result.\n   108\t    event RaffleResolved(uint256 indexed requestId, uint128 indexed winningEntry, Status indexed result);\n   109\t\n   110\t    /// @notice Emitted when the raffle enters the full-refund branch.\n   111\t    /// @param finalizer Address that enabled refunds.\n   112\t    /// @param remainingRefundLiability Raw six-decimal quote-token units initially available for ticket refunds.\n   113\t    event RefundsEnabled(address indexed finalizer, uint256 remainingRefundLiability);\n   114\t\n   115\t    /// @notice Emitted when the winning ticket is proven and all terminal quote-token liabilities are allocated.\n   116\t    /// @param ticketId Ticket proven to contain the selected winning entry.\n   117\t    /// @param settler Address that performed permissionless settlement.\n   118\t    /// @param result Final `NftWon` or `CashWon` result.\n   119\t    /// @param cashAmount Raw six-decimal quote-token units allocated to the cash winner; zero for `NftWon`.\n   120\t    /// @param protocolFee Raw six-decimal quote-token units allocated to the treasury, rounded down from gross sales.\n   121\t    /// @param sponsorAmount Raw six-decimal quote-token units allocated to the sponsor recipient as the remainder.\n   122\t    event WinningTicketSettled(\n   123\t        uint256 indexed ticketId,\n   124\t        address indexed settler,\n   125\t        Status indexed result,\n   126\t        uint256 cashAmount,\n   127\t        uint256 protocolFee,\n   128\t        uint256 sponsorAmount\n   129\t    );\n   130\t\n   131\t    /// @notice Emitted when the winning ticket owner burns the ticket and receives the corresponding prize.\n   132\t    /// @param ticketId Burned winning ticket ID.\n   133\t    /// @param winner Ticket owner that received the prize at redemption time.\n   134\t    /// @param result Final `NftWon` or `CashWon` result.\n   135\t    /// @param cashAmount Raw six-decimal quote-token units paid for `CashWon`; zero for `NftWon`.\n   136\t    /// @param prizeToken ERC-721 prize contract for `NftWon`; the zero address for `CashWon`.\n   137\t    /// @param prizeTokenId ERC-721 prize token ID for `NftWon`; zero for `CashWon`.\n   138\t    event WinningTicketRedeemed(\n   139\t        uint256 indexed ticketId,\n   140\t        address indexed winner,\n   141\t        Status indexed result,\n   142\t        uint256 cashAmount,\n   143\t        address prizeToken,\n   144\t        uint256 prizeTokenId\n   145\t    );\n   146\t\n   147\t    /// @notice Emitted when an owner burns one or more tickets for a full quote-token refund.\n   148\t    /// @param owner Ticket owner that burned the tickets and received the refund.\n   149\t    /// @param ticketQuantity Number of tickets burned in this transaction.\n   150\t    /// @param entryQuantity Aggregate number of entries represented by the burned tickets.\n   151\t    /// @param amount Raw six-decimal quote-token units refunded, equal to `entryQuantity * ENTRY_PRICE`.\n   152\t    /// @param remainingRefundLiability Raw six-decimal quote-token units still claimable after this refund.\n   153\t    event TicketsRefunded(\n   154\t        address indexed owner,\n   155\t        uint256 ticketQuantity,\n   156\t        uint256 entryQuantity,\n   157\t        uint256 amount,\n   158\t        uint256 remainingRefundLiability\n   159\t    );\n   160\t\n   161\t    /// @notice Emitted when the complete current sponsor balance is released to its immutable recipient.\n   162\t    /// @param caller Address that triggered the permissionless release.\n   163\t    /// @param recipient Immutable sponsor recipient that received the payment.\n   164\t    /// @param amount Raw six-decimal quote-token units paid.\n   165\t    event SponsorProceedsReleased(address indexed caller, address indexed recipient, uint256 amount);\n   166\t\n   167\t    /// @notice Emitted when the complete current protocol-fee balance is released to the immutable treasury.\n   168\t    /// @param caller Address that triggered the permissionless release.\n   169\t    /// @param treasury Immutable protocol treasury that received the payment.\n   170\t    /// @param amount Raw six-decimal quote-token units paid.\n   171\t    event ProtocolFeesReleased(address indexed caller, address indexed treasury, uint256 amount);\n   172\t\n   173\t    /// @notice Emitted when the escrowed prize is returned after a cash result or refund transition.\n   174\t    /// @param caller Address that triggered the permissionless release.\n   175\t    /// @param recipient Immutable sponsor recipient that received the prize.\n   176\t    /// @param prizeToken ERC-721 contract of the returned prize.\n   177\t    /// @param prizeTokenId Token ID of the returned prize.\n   178\t    event SponsorPrizeReleased(\n   179\t        address indexed caller, address indexed recipient, address indexed prizeToken, uint256 prizeTokenId\n   180\t    );\n   181\t\n   182\t    // Errors\n   183\t\n   184\t    /// @notice Raised when a caller other than the immutable factory attempts clone initialization.\n   185\t    error OnlyFactory();\n   186\t\n   187\t    /// @notice Raised when initialization is attempted more than once or on the locked implementation.\n   188\t    error AlreadyInitialized();\n   189\t\n   190\t    /// @notice Raised when a required address is the zero address.\n   191\t    error ZeroAddress();\n   192\t\n   193\t    /// @notice Raised when an operation is unavailable in the current lifecycle state.\n   194\t    /// @param actual Current raffle status.\n   195\t    error InvalidStatus(Status actual);\n   196\t\n   197\t    /// @notice Raised when an ERC-721 receiver callback does not exactly match the configured factory prize deposit.\n   198\t    /// @param token ERC-721 contract that invoked the receiver callback.\n   199\t    /// @param tokenId Token ID supplied by the callback.\n   200\t    /// @param from Address identified as the previous token owner.\n   201\t    /// @param operator Address identified as the transfer operator.\n   202\t    error UnexpectedPrize(address token, uint256 tokenId, address from, address operator);\n   203\t\n   204\t    /// @notice Raised when an entry purchase is submitted at or after the exclusive sale end.\n   205\t    /// @param endTime Exclusive sale-end Unix timestamp, in seconds.\n   206\t    /// @param currentTime Current block Unix timestamp, in seconds.\n   207\t    error SaleEnded(uint256 endTime, uint256 currentTime);\n   208\t\n   209\t    /// @notice Raised when an entry ticket would be minted to the zero address.\n   210\t    error InvalidRecipient();\n   211\t\n   212\t    /// @notice Raised when a purchase requests no entries.\n   213\t    error ZeroEntryCount();\n   214\t\n   215\t    /// @notice Raised when a purchase would exceed the `uint128` global entry-number representation.\n   216\t    /// @param totalEntries Current global sold-entry count.\n   217\t    /// @param requestedEntries Prospective entry count requested by the purchase.\n   218\t    error TotalEntriesOverflow(uint128 totalEntries, uint128 requestedEntries);\n   219\t\n   220\t    /// @notice Raised when a refund batch is empty or exceeds the bounded ticket limit.\n    80\t     * understand this adds an external call which potentially creates a reentrancy vulnerability.\n    81\t     *\n    82\t     * Requirements:\n    83\t     *\n    84\t     * - `from` cannot be the zero address.\n    85\t     * - `to` cannot be the zero address.\n    86\t     * - `tokenId` token must be owned by `from`.\n    87\t     * - If the caller is not `from`, it must be approved to move this token by either {approve} or {setApprovalForAll}.\n    88\t     *\n    89\t     * Emits a {Transfer} event.\n    90\t     */\n    91\t    function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 tokenId) external;\n    92\t\n    93\t    /**\n    94\t     * @dev Gives permission to `to` to transfer `tokenId` token to another account.\n    95\t     * The approval is cleared when the token is transferred.\n    96\t     *\n    97\t     * Only a single account can be approved at a time, so approving the zero address clears previous approvals.\n    98\t     *\n    99\t     * Requirements:\n   100\t     *\n   101\t     * - The caller must own the token or be an approved operator.\n   102\t     * - `tokenId` must exist.\n   103\t     *\n   104\t     * Emits an {Approval} event.\n   105\t     */\n   106\t    function approve(address to, uint256 tokenId) external;\n   107\t\n   108\t    /**\n   109\t     * @dev Approve or remove `operator` as an operator for the caller.\n   110\t     * Operators can call {transferFrom} or {safeTransferFrom} for any token owned by the caller.\n   111\t     *\n   112\t     * Requirements:\n   113\t     *\n   114\t     * - The `operator` cannot be the address zero.\n   115\t     *\n   116\t     * Emits an {ApprovalForAll} event.\n   117\t     */\n   118\t    function setApprovalForAll(address operator, bool approved) external;\n   119\t\n   120\t    /**\n   121\t     * @dev Returns the account approved for `tokenId` token.\n   122\t     *\n   123\t     * Requirements:\n   124\t     *\n   125\t     * - `tokenId` must exist.\n   126\t     */\n   127\t    function getApproved(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (address operator);\n   128\t\n   129\t    /**\n   130\t     * @dev Returns if the `operator` is allowed to manage all of the assets of `owner`.\n   131\t     *\n   132\t     * See {setApprovalForAll}\n   133\t     */\n   134\t    function isApprovedForAll(address owner, address operator) external view returns (bool);\n   135\t}\n6:import { IERC721 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol\";\n17:interface IRaffle {\n432:    function prizeToken() external view returns (IERC721 token);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"_kritt_extractor_helper\":true,\"stub\":false,\"stub_explanation\":\"\",\"results\":[{\"flow_summary\":\"An existing ticket owner successfully sets or clears that ticket's single-token approval. The inherited ERC-721 implementation verifies existence, accepts the owner directly, emits Approval, writes the caller-selected recipient into clone-local approval storage, and returns normally. A zero recipient clears approval; a nonzero recipient replaces it.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:28 Raffle - Public inheritance exposes ERC721.approve on the implementation and each fixed-target clone.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:93 ERC721.approve - ABI dispatch supplies caller-controlled to and tokenId and invokes _approve with the current sender.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/Context.sol:17 Context._msgSender - Returns msg.sender as the authorization principal.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:375 ERC721._approve(address,uint256,address) - Forwards the approval request with event emission enabled.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:383 ERC721._approve(address,uint256,address,bool) - Enters the approval validation and mutation path.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:386 ERC721._approve - Requires tokenId to have a current owner.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:426 ERC721._requireOwned - Resolves ownership and rejects a zero owner.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:146 ERC721._ownerOf - Reads the owner selected by tokenId from _owners.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:389 ERC721._approve - owner == auth satisfies the authorization boundary without consulting operator approvals.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:394 ERC721._approve - Emits Approval(owner, to, tokenId).\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:398 ERC721._approve - Stores _tokenApprovals[tokenId] = to and returns normally.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Emits Approval and writes the per-ticket approval mapping, then returns empty success data.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol\",\"flow_line\":398,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller-controlled tokenId selects _tokenApprovals[tokenId], and caller-controlled to is stored verbatim and logged; address(0) revokes while any nonzero address becomes the ticket's sole approved transferrer.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This is the privilege-changing storage sink for a transferable raffle bearer ticket. The approved address can subsequently transfer control of the ticket and its associated refund or winning claim, so the ownership check and exact recipient written deserve review. The path performs no external call, callback, asynchronous continuation, recipient screening, or raffle-lifecycle check.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"An operator already approved for all tickets of the current owner successfully sets or clears the selected ticket's single-token approval. After confirming that the ticket exists, the implementation crosses the collection-wide operator boundary, emits Approval, updates clone-local approval storage, and returns normally.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:28 Raffle - Public inheritance exposes ERC721.approve on the implementation and each fixed-target clone.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:93 ERC721.approve - Receives ABI-decoded, caller-controlled to and tokenId and passes msg.sender as auth.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/Context.sol:17 Context._msgSender - Preserves the external caller as the authorization principal, including under clone delegatecall.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:375 ERC721._approve(address,uint256,address) - Selects the event-emitting approval variant.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:383 ERC721._approve(address,uint256,address,bool) - Begins approval validation.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:386 ERC721._approve - Calls _requireOwned for the controlled tokenId.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:426 ERC721._requireOwned - Confirms that _ownerOf(tokenId) is nonzero.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:389 ERC721._approve - Because owner differs from auth, requires isApprovedForAll(owner, auth) to be true.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:110 ERC721.isApprovedForAll - Reads _operatorApprovals[owner][auth] and authorizes the collection-wide operator.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:394 ERC721._approve - Emits Approval(owner, to, tokenId).\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:398 ERC721._approve - Overwrites _tokenApprovals[tokenId] with to and returns normally.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"After collection-wide operator authorization, emits Approval and writes the chosen per-ticket approval recipient.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol\",\"flow_line\":389,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The controlled tokenId selects both the owner used for authorization and the approval slot; controlled to is emitted and stored unchanged, with zero clearing and nonzero granting approval. msg.sender reaches the approved-for-all lookup as auth.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"Line 389 is the delegated-authorization boundary permitting an owner-designated global operator to retarget a particular raffle ticket's transfer authority. Because tickets are bearer claims, both the global-operator lookup and the ensuing write at line 398 are security-sensitive. A mere single-token approved address does not satisfy this boundary.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"For an existing ticket that the caller neither owns nor globally operates, approval is rejected. Ownership resolution succeeds, but the owner comparison and approved-for-all lookup both fail, causing ERC721InvalidApprover and rolling back without an event or state change.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:28 Raffle - The inherited public approve selector dispatches into ERC721 code.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:93 ERC721.approve - Accepts controlled to and tokenId and supplies msg.sender as auth.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/Context.sol:17 Context._msgSender - Resolves the immediate caller used for authorization.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:375 ERC721._approve(address,uint256,address) - Forwards to the event-emitting approval variant.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:386 ERC721._approve - Requires and obtains the current owner of controlled tokenId.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:389 ERC721._approve - Finds owner != auth and isApprovedForAll(owner, auth) == false; it deliberately does not accept an existing single-token approval.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:390 ERC721._approve - Reverts with ERC721InvalidApprover(auth), preventing the event and storage write.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Reverts with ERC721InvalidApprover(msg.sender); no approval event or mutation survives.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol\",\"flow_line\":389,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller-controlled tokenId chooses the ticket owner against whom msg.sender is checked. The terminal custom error contains msg.sender; controlled to is discarded before reaching the event or approval mapping.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This authorization boundary prevents callers—including addresses holding only the current per-token approval—from replacing that approval. It deserves review because failure here would let an unauthorized party redirect transfer authority over a bearer ticket.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"For an unminted or already burned ticketId, approval terminates at the existence check. The owner mapping returns zero and ERC721NonexistentToken(tokenId) is raised before authorization, event emission, or mutation.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:28 Raffle - The implementation and clones expose inherited ERC721.approve; the locked implementation also reaches this path because it has no minted tickets.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:93 ERC721.approve - Receives the caller-selected to and tokenId and invokes _approve.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:375 ERC721._approve(address,uint256,address) - Selects the event-emitting approval path.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:383 ERC721._approve(address,uint256,address,bool) - Starts validation before any write.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:386 ERC721._approve - Calls _requireOwned(tokenId).\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:426 ERC721._requireOwned - Resolves the owner for the controlled identifier.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:146 ERC721._ownerOf - Reads _owners[tokenId] and returns address(0) for an unminted or burned ticket.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:428 ERC721._requireOwned - Detects the zero owner.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:429 ERC721._requireOwned - Reverts with ERC721NonexistentToken(tokenId).\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Reverts with ERC721NonexistentToken(tokenId) before authorization or state mutation.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol\",\"flow_line\":429,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller-controlled tokenId is used as the owner-mapping key and becomes the terminal custom-error argument. Controlled to is not emitted, stored, or otherwise used after the failed existence check.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This is the existence boundary that prevents approvals from being created for nonexistent or consumed raffle tickets. It also covers direct calls to the ticketless implementation and calls using never-minted or burned IDs; no external calls or asynchronous work occur.\"}]}"}}
